# Keep the frontend build context lean; deps are installed fresh in the image.
#
# EVERY pattern is `**/`-prefixed. A bare `node_modules` or `*.key` matches only at the CONTEXT
# ROOT — docker does not apply it recursively. Measured with a probe image: `sub/secrets/leaked.key`
# was copied in while the root-level equivalent was excluded, so the credential lines below read as
# a guard while protecting only the one directory a credential is least likely to be sitting in.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.mf
# `.ideable-ui` is a TRACKED SYMLINK to the repo-root reusable.ui, so a fresh clone resolves the
# `file:` dependency with no bootstrap step. It must not enter the build context: a symlink pointing
# four levels above a SOURCES-rooted context is dangling there, and the Dockerfile creates the real
# directory itself from the `ideable_ui` named build context.
**/.ideable-ui
# Secrets must never enter a build context — no context in the repo excluded them before.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/.DS_Store
